{"name":"Grass Court","hex":"#088d46","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grass court","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tennis court with a grass surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grass_court"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grass court","blocks":[{"text":"A grass court is one of the types of tennis court on which the sport of tennis, originally known as \"lawn tennis\", is played. Grass courts are made of grasses in different compositions depending on the tournament."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Federer_Wimbledon_2006.JPG/330px-Federer_Wimbledon_2006.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grass_court","wikidata":"Q1151291"},{"title":"Grass","blocks":[{"text":"Grass refers to various families of plants. The three major families of grasslike plants are true grasses (Poaceae), sedges (Cyperaceae), and rushes (Juncaceae). Lawns and pasturelands are typically composed of true grasses, five of which cover 46% of the world's arable land: rice, wheat, maize, barley, and sugar cane."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Poa_annua.jpg/330px-Poa_annua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grass","wikidata":"Q643352"},{"title":"Court","blocks":[{"text":"A court is an institution, often a government entity, with the authority to adjudicate legal disputes between parties and administer justice in civil, criminal, and administrative matters in accordance with the rule of law."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Microcosm_of_London_Plate_058_-_Old_Bailey_edited.jpg/330px-Microcosm_of_London_Plate_058_-_Old_Bailey_edited.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Court","wikidata":"Q41487"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://th